    <briefdescription>
<para>This structure contains the parameters for the USER eFUSE key provisioning command. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>USER_EFUSE_KEY_0 is always programmed in black form. USER_EFUSE_KEY_1 accepts both black and red via KeyForm. Red USER key 1 is usable by PLM and ASU; black USER key 0 and black USER key 1 are subsystem-exclusive, so choose black provisioning with the end use case in mind. The key source is selected explicitly via KeySource:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XASU_PROVISION_KEY_SOURCE_ASU_GENERATED: the ASU generates the key with the TRNG; KeyId and KeyAddr must both be zero. This is the only source permitted for USER_EFUSE_KEY_0.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_PROVISION_KEY_SOURCE_VAULT: KeyId selects an AKV key (KeyAddr must be zero).</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_PROVISION_KEY_SOURCE_USER_BUFFER: KeyAddr supplies a raw key buffer (KeyId must be zero). </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
